// @decisions: D-457, D-617
> import std::string
> const big: String = string::repeat("abc", 9_000_000_000_000_000_000)
error[E0076]: evaluating the constant `big` used more than the memory limit of 1GiB
 --> <repl:2>:1:7
  |
1 | const big: String = string::repeat("abc", 9_000_000_000_000_000_000)
  |       ^^^ this constant is computed at compile time
  |
  = note: the limit counts the heap bytes that the evaluation keeps live at once
  = help: compute less at compile time, or raise `memory-limit` in the `[const-eval]` table of `cheby.toml`

